        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-10-07 06:02:09.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(2 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good; the conversions are correct and every long option in the touched handlers still has a matching case. Two optional points are inline for whenever the patch is next refreshed, so there's no need to re-spin for them. On its own this change leaves jt_show_net(), the case named in the ticket, still returning 0 for an unknown option; that fix is only in 69344, and the two changes aren't linked in Gerrit. Could they be squashed or put in one relation chain so they land together? If the patch is refreshed, a small sanity-lnet check that `lnetctl route show --bogus` and similar commands now exit non-zero would keep this from regressing.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
